    <string name="tc_dxvk_title">DXVK config</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_hint">Options of dxvk.conf for the DXVK that Hangover installs. They are sent as DXVK_CONFIG (DXVK 2.4 or newer) and apply the next time the container starts or a Shortcut is launched. A per-Shortcut DXVK_CONFIG in its Env settings replaces this value.</string>
    <string name="tc_d3d_dxvk">Use DXVK (Direct3D to Vulkan)</string>
    <string name="tc_d3d_dxvk_hint">Off = WineD3D (Direct3D to OpenGL). Writes the DllOverrides of d3d8, d3d9, d3d10core, d3d11 and dxgi in the Wine prefix as native (DXVK) or builtin (WineD3D), like the Enable/Disable DXVK commands. DXVK must be installed in the prefix (the Hangover script does that). If the container is not running, the prefix is updated the next time a Shortcut launches.</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_apply">Send DXVK_CONFIG</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_apply_hint">Turn off to leave DXVK completely at its own defaults.</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_tune">Memory-saving defaults</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_tune_hint">Low device/shared memory, one compiler thread, no pipeline library and no state cache. Fixes black screens on small-memory GPUs such as Adreno 610. Your own values below override it.</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_present">Present mode</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_present_hint">Sets dxgi.syncInterval, d3d9.presentInterval and dxvk.tearFree together: FIFO, relaxed FIFO, mailbox or immediate.</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_preview">DXVK_CONFIG=%1$s</string>
    <string name="tc_dxvk_preview_none">Nothing is sent: DXVK runs with its own defaults.</string>
